                <pb facs="0337" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1057a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-01T13:00:00-05:00">February 1, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>16. For your information. Press reports indicate that Japanese press has widely
                    carried stories affirming comprehensive political negotiations between Grew and
                    Hirota and between Hull and Saito.</p>
                <p>Interrogated by press correspondents this morning, the Secretary of State said
                    there were no new developments in relations between the United States and
                    countries of the Far East; and Departmental officers have informally explained
                    to correspondents that there have been held numerous conferences with regard to
                    particular questions of trade but no conferences on political matters have been
                    held or been suggested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
